.Dd September 22, 2026
.Dt CHPASS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm chpass ,
.Nm chfn ,
.Nm chsh
.Nd change a user's full name or shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm chpass
.Op Fl f Ar full-name
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Ar user
.Nm chfn
.Op Fl f Ar full-name
.Op Ar user
.Nm chsh
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
edits the account of
.Ar user ,
or the caller's when no user is given.
.Pp
On NextBSD an account lives in one of two places, and
.Nm
edits whichever holds it:
.Bl -bullet
.It
A proper user is a record in
.Pa Users.plist
under
.Pa /Local/Library/DirectoryServices
.Po
or under
.Pa /Network/Library/DirectoryServices
on a machine joined to a directory server
.Pc .
.Fl f
sets its
.Va realName
and
.Fl s
its
.Va shell .
With neither, the record is printed.
The other fields of a directory user
.Pq uid, gid, groups, password
belong to
.Xr dscli 8
and
.Xr passwd 1 .
.It
Root and the system users are in
.Pa /etc/master.passwd .
For them FreeBSD's
.Nm ,
kept at
.Pa /usr/libexec/bsd/chpass ,
is run with the same arguments and behaves as documented there.
.El
.Pp
A user may change their own full name and shell after typing their
password; root may change anyone's.
A user's new shell must be listed in
.Pa /etc/shells ;
root is only warned.
On a joined client the accounts in use are the server's and
.Nm
refuses to edit them.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Network/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist" -compact
.It Pa /Local/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist
directory users
.It Pa /Network/Library/DirectoryServices/Users.plist
the server's users, when joined
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
root and the system users
.It Pa /etc/shells
the shells a user may choose
.It Pa /usr/libexec/bsd/chpass
FreeBSD's
.Nm ,
for system accounts
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr shells 5 ,
.Xr dscli 8 ,
.Xr pw 8 ,
.Xr vipw 8
